#compdef lvm lvchange lvconvert lvcreate lvdisplay lvextend lvmconfig lvmdevices lvmdiskscan lvreduce lvremove lvrename lvresize lvs lvscan pvchange pvck pvcreate pvdisplay pvmove pvremove pvresize pvs pvscan vgcfgbackup vgcfgrestore vgchange vgck vgconvert vgcreate vgdisplay vgexport vgextend vgimport vgimportclone vgimportdevices vgmerge vgmknodes vgreduce vgremove vgrename vgs vgscan vgsplit
# Option names, value-taking options and enumerated values (y|n, --type ...)
# are parsed from `<command> --longhelp` of the local LVM. PV/VG/LV names come
# from the read-only reports pvs/vgs/lvs; candidate disks from /sys.
local tool=${words[1]:t} lvm_bin= prev= option= word help line type= snapshot=no thin=no skip=no
local -i start=2 i
local -a tools w options value_options fields positionals
tools=(lvchange lvconvert lvcreate lvdisplay lvextend lvmconfig lvmdevices lvmdiskscan lvreduce
    lvremove lvrename lvresize lvs lvscan pvchange pvck pvcreate pvdisplay pvmove pvremove pvresize
    pvs pvscan vgcfgbackup vgcfgrestore vgchange vgck vgconvert vgcreate vgdisplay vgexport vgextend
    vgimport vgimportclone vgimportdevices vgmerge vgmknodes vgreduce vgremove vgrename vgs vgscan vgsplit)

if [[ $tool == lvm ]]; then
    lvm_bin=${(Q)words[1]}
    [[ $lvm_bin == '~/'* ]] && lvm_bin=$HOME/${lvm_bin#'~/'}
    if (( CURRENT == 2 )); then
        compadd -a tools
        compadd -- config devtypes dumpconfig formats fullreport help lastlog lvpoll segtypes systemid tags version
        return
    fi
    tool=${(Q)words[2]}
    start=3
    if [[ $tool == help ]]; then
        (( CURRENT == 3 )) && compadd -a tools
        return
    fi
elif whence lvm >/dev/null; then
    lvm_bin=lvm
fi
(( CURRENT > start )) && prev=${(Q)words[CURRENT-1]}

help=$(_mini_lvm_run $tool --longhelp 2>/dev/null | _mini_lvm_parse_help $tool)
[[ -n $help ]] || help=$(_mini_lvm_run $tool --help 2>/dev/null | _mini_lvm_parse_help $tool)
for line in ${(f)help}; do
    fields=(${=line})
    options+=($fields[1])
    [[ $fields[2] == value ]] && value_options+=($fields[1])
done
# Minimal fallback when the tool cannot print its help.
(( $#options )) || options=(-h --help -v --verbose -y --yes -t --test --version)

# Option value: "--opt value" or "--opt=value".
if [[ $PREFIX == --*=* ]]; then
    option=${PREFIX%%=*}
    compset -P 1 '*='
elif (( ${value_options[(Ie)$prev]} )); then
    option=$prev
fi
if [[ -n $option ]]; then
    fields=(${=${(M)${(f)help}:#$option *}})
    local arg=$fields[3]
    local -a enum=($fields[4,-1])
    case $option in
        -f|--file) _files; return ;;
        -o|--options|-O|--sort)
            if [[ $tool == (pvs|vgs|lvs|fullreport) ]]; then
                # Field lists are comma separated; complete the last item, keep +/-.
                compset -P '*,'
                compset -P '[+-]'
                w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_run $tool -o help 2>&1 | awk '$2 == "-" {print $1}')"})
                compadd -S '' -a w
                return
            fi ;;
        --units) enum=(h H b B s S k K m M g G t T p P e E r R) ;;
        --devices) arg=PV_disk ;;
    esac
    if (( $#enum )); then
        w=($enum)
    else
        case $arg in
            VG|VG\|*) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names vg)"}) ;;
            LV|LV\|*) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names lv)"}) ;;
            PV_disk) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names pv; _mini_lvm_disks)"}) ;;
            PV|PV\|*) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names pv)"}) ;;
        esac
    fi
    compadd -a w
    return
fi

if [[ $PREFIX == -* ]]; then
    compadd -a options
    return
fi

# Positional arguments, skipping options and their values.
for (( i = start; i < CURRENT; i++ )); do
    word=${(Q)words[i]}
    if [[ $skip == yes ]]; then skip=no; continue; fi
    case $word in
        -s|--snapshot) snapshot=yes ;;
        -T|--thin) thin=yes ;;
    esac
    if [[ $word == -* ]]; then
        (( ${value_options[(Ie)$word]} )) && skip=yes
        continue
    fi
    positionals+=($word)
done

# Argument types by position (counted from 0).
case $tool:$#positionals in
    pvs:*|pvdisplay:*|pvchange:*|pvck:*|pvremove:*|pvresize:*|pvmove:*) type=pv ;;
    pvcreate:*|vgimportclone:*) type=disk ;;
    vgcreate:0|vgrename:1|vgsplit:1) type= ;;
    vgcreate:*|vgextend:[1-9]*) type=disk ;;
    vgreduce:[1-9]*|vgsplit:[2-9]*) type=pv ;;
    vgcfgrestore:0|vgmerge:[01]|vgsplit:0|vgextend:0|vgreduce:0|vgrename:0) type=vg ;;
    vgs:*|vgdisplay:*|vgchange:*|vgck:*|vgremove:*|vgexport:*|vgimport:*|vgcfgbackup:*|vgmknodes:*|vgconvert:*|vgimportdevices:*) type=vg ;;
    lvs:*|lvdisplay:*) type=vglv ;;
    lvchange:*|lvremove:*|lvconvert:0|lvextend:0|lvreduce:0|lvresize:0) type=lv ;;
    lvconvert:*|lvextend:*|lvreduce:*|lvresize:*) type=pv ;;
    lvrename:0) type=vglv ;;
    lvrename:1) [[ $positionals[1] == */* ]] || type=lvinvg ;;
    lvcreate:0)
        if [[ $snapshot == yes ]]; then type=lv
        elif [[ $thin == yes ]]; then type=vglv
        else type=vg
        fi ;;
    lvcreate:*) [[ $snapshot == yes ]] || type=pv ;;
esac
case $type in
    pv) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names pv)"}) ;;
    disk)
        w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_disks)"})
        # Other paths, e.g. /dev/disk/by-id/...
        [[ $PREFIX == */* ]] && _files ;;
    vg) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names vg)"}) ;;
    lv) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names lv)"}) ;;
    vglv) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names vg; _mini_lvm_names lv)"}) ;;
    lvinvg) w=(${(f)"$(_mini_lvm_names lv $positionals[1])"}) ;;
    *) return 1 ;;
esac
compadd -a w
